# The website does NOT need a key of its own. It shares the desktop app's
# PostHog project, and that key already lives in the repo-root `.env` as
# `WRITER_POSTHOG_KEY`. The website build does not load that file on its own,
# so source it first — from the repository root:
#
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   vp run website#build
#
# This file is only for pointing the *website alone* somewhere else — a
# scratch project, a different region — without touching the app. Copy it to
# apps/website/.env, which Vite loads automatically, and set what you need.
# Either variable takes precedence over its `WRITER_` counterpart; leave it
# blank or absent to fall back. See docs/website-analytics.md.

# Public PostHog project key (a `phc_...` value — publishable, not a secret).
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=

# Ingestion host. Falls back to WRITER_POSTHOG_HOST, then to
# https://us.i.posthog.com.
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com
